# Pelican fresh world

Every Pelican deploy deletes the dedicated-server world. The next start creates a new one.

- Default is `python scripts/deploy_server.py --from-local`, including the Pelican step inside `release.py`. After the server stops, the script deletes the `level-name` folder (usually `world`, plus leftover `world_nether` / `world_the_end`).
- Pass `--keep-world` only when the user explicitly says to keep the existing world.
- `--share-only` does not touch the panel, so it does not delete a world.
- Do not mention the panel or join address in GitHub-facing copy.
